        'USA',
      ],
      timeline: [
        '1980s: First documented in American casino circles.',
        '1990s: Spread to European poker rooms and tournaments.',
        '2000s: Pot Limit Omaha (PLO) becomes the dominant variant online.',
        "Present: Second only to Hold'em in tournament and cash-game popularity.",
      ],
      evolution: 'Omaha High-Low 8-or-Better (Omaha/8) split the pot between best high and best qualifying low hand, adding strategic depth.',
      cultural: "Known as 'the game of the nuts' because hand values run closer; draws and redraws are frequent.",
